    "searchCoverage": "Official agent instructions require POST /api/v1/auth/token with {api_key} to mint a JWT, then Authorization: Bearer <access_token> on GET /users/me and other authenticated routes. Tokens expire after 24 hours. Pinned OpenConnector performs that exchange before every call. Current public instructions also document https://thecolony.ai while the pinned source hardcodes https://thecolony.cc/api/v1. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found no qualifying current unresolved The Colony compromise. Native HTTP templates can send a static API key header but cannot POST for a JWT and then use the returned token.",
    "incidents": [],
    "remainingGates": [
      "credentials: official and pinned auth is a two-step token exchange (POST /auth/token with api_key, then Bearer JWT). Native templates have no derive/token-exchange block for this shape; sending the col_ key as Bearer would not match the official API.",
      "live authentication unverified"
    ],
    "waiverAuthority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13 permits historical non-China incident coverage."
